Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:26:35 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 312/407] Unified: "Turns in place" - a part of an assembly
 turns about a round face, held by the ground

A joint needed two parts: a crank could not be made to turn on the ground,
and fixing it to the ground stopped it (engine field test 0.7.3: a case
part was made only to hold the crank). One round face (or circle) of a
part of an assembly offers "Turns in place" on the bar: a revolute joint
to the assembly's origin where the part is now. "Turn to an angle" in the
joint turns it.

Test: FreeCADCmd -t TestAssemblySolve

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
